1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,697
How do you turn Twitch clips into YouTube Shorts?

2
00:00:03,750 --> 00:00:08,653
For one clip, Twitch can already make a portrait version and share it to Shorts.

3
00:00:08,653 --> 00:00:11,902
For a whole stream, paste the Twitch VOD into ClipMe.

4
00:00:11,902 --> 00:00:15,334
It ranks the moments and cuts captioned vertical Shorts.

5
00:00:16,284 --> 00:00:21,100
Twitch's sharing works one clip at a time, and you still have to find the moment.

6
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:22,705
ClipMe ranks the whole VOD.

7
00:00:23,655 --> 00:00:29,244
It reads Twitch chat, and chat activity is one of the signals ClipMe uses to rank each moment.

8
00:00:30,195 --> 00:00:35,507
Every clip comes out captioned in 9:16, and Pro adds 4:5 and 1:1.

9
00:00:36,457 --> 00:00:39,960
See how Twitch VODs become Shorts at clipme.com.

10
00:00:39,960 --> 00:00:42,004
Paste a VOD and try it free.

